id: pm-ob9z4y
title: "Prose-asserted relationships are unmeasured: 1,750 identifier pairs named in item text carry no edge in any direction, and nothing counts the gap"
description: "Item descriptions, comments, notes and learnings name 8,995 resolvable identifiers; 1,750 of the distinct pairs hold no dependency edge of any kind, so the prose copy of the relationship graph is larger than the copy every graph query reads. Deliver a parity census, a reviewed exemption ledger for ledger surfaces and negative statements, and a ratcheted ceiling in quality:static so the gap can only shrink."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: ci-gate,context-management,graph,measurement-ratchet,tracker-governance
created_at: "2026-08-10T12:12:23.720Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-20T21:14:52.647Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-20T21:14:51.943Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-20T21:14:51.943Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: "A census resolves prose identifier mentions to real items and reports pairs holding no edge of any kind, counts first with a capped sample; Ledger surfaces, negative-statement phrasings and analysis subjects are exemptible with a recorded reason; an exemption is data, never a silent skip; The unexempted gap is declared as a ceiling so a pass may shrink it or leave it but never grow it, with a negative control proving the ceiling fails when exceeded; The gate runs in quality:static so a new item that names work it does not depend on fails before merge, not at release; The census is bounded in tokens and latency and stays within budget at million-item scale, reading each item once"
goal: Provable history
objective: Make graph completeness a measured property of the record rather than a periodic discovery
value: "Turns a 1,750-pair blind spot into an owned number that shrinks monotonically, without fabricating a single edge"
impact: "Every graph algorithm, context assembly and impact query currently reads an incomplete graph and cannot report by how much"
outcome: The unexempted prose-versus-edge gap is enforced as a ceiling that a productive pass cannot grow
why_now: "Measured 2026-08-10 during the strategic-ladder wave, which shrank the gap from 2,333 to 1,750 and showed the remainder is not safely automatable"
parent: pm-96h7
reviewer: maintainer-review
risk: medium
confidence: high
sprint: 2026-w33
reporter: maintainer-agent
environment: "pm 2026.8.10, 2412 items, 10042 stored edges"
resolution: "Added a public single-pass prose_edge_gap assurance source with canonical-ID resolution, reasoned exemptions, exact explicit/implicit partitions, bounded contributor samples, cost receipts, CLI contract publication, a live monotone ceiling, and a million-item benchmark."
expected_result: "All-status prose references are measured against structured relationships with reviewable exemptions, exact counts and partitions, bounded agent-readable output, a failing ceiling negative control, and million-item performance evidence."
actual_result: "graph-composition passes with 1,343 unexempted gaps at ceiling 1,343, explicit_subject=1,216, implicit_subject=127, 25 sampled contributors, and cost 85,551. The million-item public-SDK benchmark reports zero gaps in 6.412s at cost 2,999,998; all linked tests and repository gates pass."
component: "scripts/quality, graph audit"
