comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-11T13:58:00.698Z","harness:claude-code","Cross-reference 2026-08-11: this item owns counting the prose-named pairs that carry no edge. A promotion experiment recorded in full on pm-wmf72c establishes the precision ceiling for the obvious rule shape. At a same-sentence cue-immediately-before-identifier threshold the rule yields 8 candidates over the whole corpus and all 8 are false positives, because a cue identifies the relationship kind and object but never its subject, and in tracker prose the subject is usually a third identifier in the same sentence. So the 1,750-pair gap this item measures is not closable by a cue-and-object rule at any window size. The measurement this item owns should therefore report the pairs partitioned by whether the sentence contains an explicit subject identifier, because that partition is what decides how much of the gap is mechanically promotable at all."
  "2026-08-20T19:59:25.548Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-20: live tracker and GitHub inventory found no duplicate implementation item. This branch will deliver a single-pass SDK census over descriptions, body, comments, notes, and learnings; reasoned exemptions; capped agent-readable samples; assurance integration; latency/token bounds; and a failing negative control."
  "2026-08-20T20:56:57.560Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: prose-edge-gap source is contract-tested across every prose surface, scalar/structured links, canonical/self/unknown resolution, deduplication, explicit/implicit partitions, reasoned exemptions, contributor caps, validation errors, cost receipts, and verdict propagation. The million-item linked-chain benchmark passes with zero gaps in 7.013s, cost 2,999,998, and ~824 MB peak RSS. Live graph-composition observes 1,343 gaps at ceiling 1,343, partitions explicit=1,216/implicit=127, and only 25 sampled contributors."
  "2026-08-20T21:14:49.394Z","harness:codex","Final linked-test evidence: tracker-context execution passed 3/3 linked commands: million-node benchmark, full quality:static, and focused assurance suites. Latest benchmark receipt: 1,000,000 nodes, 0 gaps, exact partitions 0/0, cost 2,999,998, duration 6.412s, peak RSS 824,561,664 bytes."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-20T20:56:59.286Z","harness:codex","A scalable prose-edge census can stay exact and token-bounded by collecting canonical identifiers, structured pairs, and prose mentions in one item pass, resolving afterward, deduplicating holder-target pairs, and capping only contributor samples—not counts or partitions."
